carries over in every timed kit).\n    33\t**D17 post-run:** every mode asked only `pcm_s16le` (no transcode delivered); the D17-night prebuild covered the audio\n    34\tflavor and `media-video-streams`. Lesson: each new family lands under an ABSTRACT fmt word with tool (ffprobe) vocabulary.\n    35\t**D18 \"Frame of Reference\" = video** (`media.primary_video_dimensions` of one h264+aac `video-001.mp4` -> `320x180`; id\n    36\t`d18-video-001-media-...`: same fmt `media`, family `video`). Prebuilt `media_video.py` answered it in the race probe\n    37\t(~5 s). Flavor: \"Clips, previews, and screen recordings have been mixed together. Use stream geometry to identify\n    38\toriginals, crops, and the recording that could not have come from the claimed device.\" -- none of it was asked; all\n    39\tgeometry sources agreed (stsd = tkhd = SPS, identity matrix, SAR 1:1) in every set. Audio stayed exactly one day deep\n    40\t(D17 codec only), so the `media` namespace is moving ONE stream property per day. Next plausible (D19-D21): more ffprobe\n    41\tgeometry (`primary_video_codec_name`, rotation/displaymatrix, SAR/DAR, coded vs display size after SPS/clap crop), the\n    42\tclaimed DEVICE (QuickTime mdta make/model/software, `©mak/©mod`, Android keys, handler/encoder/compressor name), stills\n    43\tasked through `media.*` (\"previews\": ffprobe opens JPEG/PNG as a 1-stream video -- lib answers `none` today!), a\n    44\tgeometry synthesis (originals vs crops, aspect groups, the impossible-device file), then a NEW abstract namespace\n    45\t(`image.*`, `archive.*`, `log.*`/`event.*`, `disk.*`).\n    46\t**D19 \"Little Endian on the Prairie\" = ELF** (`elf.e_machine_u16_hex` of one `collector-001.elf` -> `0x003e`; id\n    47\t`d19-elf-001-elf-...`: plain fmt `elf`, family `elf` -- NOT an abstract `binary.*`). Prebuilt `lib.meta` fmt `elf`\n    48\tanswered it in the race probe (~13 s). Same x86-64 LSB ELF64 in every mode/set; the timed kit pools it with the D9 G