{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q1BMs9s6hpiggidATmRxqN","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# metadata-forensics — coverage atlas (as of D19 post-run, 2026-10-19)\n59:## 1. Atlas\n185:## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n245:## Readiness gaps\n# metadata-forensics — coverage atlas (as of D19 post-run, 2026-10-19)\n\nWhat the lane might ask next vs what we can already answer. Grammar is always `Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`;\nid `dNN-<fmt>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>`; the registry is `lib.meta` (built-ins = verified/speculative, plus\n`lib/meta/prebuilt/*.py` speculative modules ranked in `lib/meta/prebuilt/TARGETS.json`). Check what exists with\n`python3 -c \"import lib.meta as m; print(sorted(k for k in m.known_fields() if k[0]=='<fmt>'))\"`.\n\n**Status:** `seen Dn` = GM-verified that day (built-in, verified tier) · `prebuilt <module>` = speculative extractor\nregistered (gate passed) · `partial` = some sibling fields registered · `gap` = nothing registered (TARGET name given\nwhen one exists but is not built yet).\n**Tools:** (I) = installed (`.venv/bin/python` import or on the `source bin/env.sh` PATH), (M) = missing.\nIn-window extractors may only import the prebuild gate's `ALLOWED_IMPORTS` (`hctf/prebuild.py:112`: stdlib subset +\n`pefile elftools capstone Crypto androguard pyzipper lib`) and may NOT call `open()` -- so Evtx / regipy / olefile /\noletools / dnfile / LnkParse3 / lief / cryptography / asn1crypto / dpkt / PIL / `sqlite3` / `mailbox` / `wave` are\nworker-only (LLM side) until the allowlist is widened. See gaps `gate-allowlist-*`.\n**Likelihood** reasoning: D9-D15 walked Windows binaries/installers/shortcuts/Office (PE -> PE version -> .NET -> MSI\n-> LNK -> OOXML); the next steps are most plausibly other Windows DFIR artifacts and legacy-Office/CFB siblings,\nplus deeper fields of already-seen families (timed kits are cumulative, D15 added cross-file synthesis).\n**D16 turned to e-mail** (`email.message_id` of one `.eml`; flavor \"replies, forwards, duplicates, reconstructed\nmessages ... stable message identities\"). PE stayed three days (D9-11) with a deeper field each day, so D17-D19 most\nplausibly ask deeper `email.*` fields (In-Reply-To / References / attachments / Received / auth) or a sibling mail\ncontainer (MBOX, Outlook MSG), then cross-message threading as a synthesis question. GM fmt word is `email`, not `eml`.\n**D17 jumped to audio instead** (`media.primary_audio_codec_name` of one PCM `.wav` -> `pcm_s16le`; id\n`d17-audio-001-media-...`: family `audio`, fmt `media`, ffprobe vocabulary). Flavor: \"Voice notes have been\ntranscoded, renamed, and embedded in mail. Determine the actual codecs, connect equivalent recordings, and find the\nstream that breaks the sender's story.\" -> D18-D20 most plausibly: the same `media.*` namespace on OTHER containers/\ncodecs (renamed `.wav` that is MP3/Ogg-Opus/M4A/AMR -- \"actual codecs\"), deeper ffprobe stream fields (sample_rate,\nchannels, duration, bit_rate, format_name, stream count), a multi-stream container where one stream disagrees\n(\"stream that breaks the story\": language/creation_time/encoder/codec), audio as a MIME attachment inside `.eml`\n(\"embedded in mail\" -- D16 + D17 combined), and a cross-recording equivalence synthesis (\"connect equivalent\nrecordings\": same INFO title / correlation id / PCM payload / duration). Video `media.*` (h264 etc.) is the next step\nafter that. Email fields remain warm (D16 family carries over in every timed kit).\n**D17 post-run:** every mode asked only `pcm_s16le` (no transcode delivered); the D17-night prebuild covered the audio\nflavor and `media-video-streams`. Lesson: each new family lands under an ABSTRACT fmt word with tool (ffprobe) vocabulary.\n**D18 \"Frame of Reference\" = video** (`media.primary_video_dimensions` of one h264+aac `video-001.mp4` -> `320x180`; id\n`d18-video-001-media-...`: same fmt `media`, family `video`). Prebuilt `media_video.py` answered it in the race probe\n(~5 s). Flavor: \"Clips, previews, and screen recordings have been mixed together. Use stream geometry to identify\noriginals, crops, and the recording that could not have come from the claimed device.\" -- none of it was asked; all\ngeometry sources agreed (stsd = tkhd = SPS, identity matrix, SAR 1:1) in every set. Audio stayed exactly one day deep\n(D17 codec only), so the `media` namespace is moving ONE stream property per day. Next plausible (D19-D21): more ffprobe","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"477ba029-865b-464a-9dbb-2d2f93cfd02a","uuid":"41ac9662-14ca-4b9e-9dc1-006073673012","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:15:54.658Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1:# metadata-forensics — coverage atlas (as of D19 post-run, 2026-10-19)\n59:## 1. Atlas\n185:## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n245:## Readiness gaps\n# metadata-forensics — coverage atlas (as of D19 post-run, 2026-10-19)\n\nWhat the lane might ask next vs what we can already answer. Grammar is always `Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`;\nid `dNN-<fmt>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>`; the registry is `lib.meta` (built-ins = verified/speculative, plus\n`lib/meta/prebuilt/*.py` speculative modules ranked in `lib/meta/prebuilt/TARGETS.json`). Check what exists with\n`python3 -c \"import lib.meta as m; print(sorted(k for k in m.known_fields() if k[0]=='<fmt>'))\"`.\n\n**Status:** `seen Dn` = GM-verified that day (built-in, verified tier) · `prebuilt <module>` = speculative extractor\nregistered (gate passed) · `partial` = some sibling fields registered · `gap` = nothing registered (TARGET name given\nwhen one exists but is not built yet).\n**Tools:** (I) = installed (`.venv/bin/python` import or on the `source bin/env.sh` PATH), (M) = missing.\nIn-window extractors may only import the prebuild gate's `ALLOWED_IMPORTS` (`hctf/prebuild.py:112`: stdlib subset +\n`pefile elftools capstone Crypto androguard pyzipper lib`) and may NOT call `open()` -- so Evtx / regi