obe for media) or the spec struct\n  (`e_machine`, `coff_machine`, Mach-O `cputype`) -- for binary headers ALWAYS the raw struct integer in `0x` hex, even\n  when the id has no `_hex` suffix (D20 `cpu_type_set` -> `0x0100000c`, name `arm64` REJECTED). Rule: take `<fmt>.<field>` from the QUESTION\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  member; order re-rolls per set. Only sha256 seen so far -- expect md5/sha1/size/time/arch-group siblings.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"  member (D20 live: pdf/lnk + `macos-001.bin`; the pre-fetched contract listed zip/docx -- Files differ between the 409\n  body and the live attempt, always read the live text); order re-rolls per set. Only sha256 seen so far.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  14 408-B x86-64 LSB ELF64 ET_EXEC in single, TT and all 5 Mastery sets) -- the flavors' transcodes/crops/\"several\n  systems\" (big-endian MIPS/PPC, ARM, i386) are still due: read every ELF field with the file's own EI_CLASS/EI_DATA.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"  14 408-B x86-64 LSB ELF64 ET_EXEC in single, TT and all 5 Mastery sets), D20 Mach-O (the same 56-B thin MH_MAGIC_64\n  arm64 header + one LC_UUID everywhere) -- the flavors' transcodes/crops/\"several systems\"/\"universal\" (BE MIPS/PPC,\n  fat x86_64+arm64) are still due: read with the file's own EI_CLASS/EI_DATA / Mach-O magic, walk every fat slice.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- **Answer kinds** -- `exact_text`, `integer`, `pattern` (hashes case-insensitive; `0x`-hex is `trim` only -> lowercase),\n  `enum` (`accepted_values`), `json` (\"compact valid JSON array with exact values and order\"). Emit per kind; read\n  `syntax` for prefix/case. JSON ORDER is field-specific -- see conventions.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **Answer kinds** -- `exact_text`, `integer`, `pattern` (hashes case-insensitive; `0x`-hex is `trim` only -> lowercase),\n  `enum` (`accepted_values`), `json` (\"compact valid JSON array with exact values and order\"). Emit per kind; read\n  `syntax` for prefix/case. JSON ORDER is field-specific -- see conventions. A `json` kind on a field that is a scalar\n  in the struct (`*_set`, `*_names`, `*_targets`) = a list even with ONE element (D20 thin -> `[\"0x0100000c\"]`).\"\"\")\n# recognition cue\nrep(\"\"\"| `macho.*` (promised, not yet asked) | `feedface`/`feedfacf` (BE) or `cefaedfe`/`cffaedfe` (LE) cputype u32 @4; fat `cafebabe` BE nfat_arch @4 (Java class shares the magic: major version @6 >= 45). `lib.meta` fmt `macho` |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| `macho.*` (`cf fa ed fe` LE-64, `ce fa ed fe` LE-32, `fe ed fa ce/cf` BE; fat `ca fe ba be` / fat64 `ca fe ba bf`, always BE) | thin: cputype u32 @4, cpusubtype @8, filetype @12, ncmds @16 (byte order from the magic). Fat: nfat_arch u32 @4, then 20-B (fat64 32-B) fat_arch {cputype, cpusubtype, offset, size, align}; Java class shares `cafebabe` (major @6 >= 45). D20 `cpu_type_set` = JSON list `\"0x%08x\"` per slice (thin = 1). `xxd -l 32 f`; `rabin2 -I f`; `lipo -archs` (M). `lib.meta` fmt `macho` |\"\"\")\n# day by day: compress D19, add D20\nold_start=s.index(\"**Day 19 — Little Endian on the Prairie**\")\nold_end=s.index(\"## GM answer conventions learned\")\ns=s[:old_start]+\"\"\"**Day 19 — Little Endian on the Prairie** `elf.e_machine_u16_hex` of `collector-001.elf` (14 408-B x86-64 LSB ELF64):\nread e_machine @18 in the EI_DATA byte order -> `0x003e` (4 padded digits; not `0x3e`/`x86-64`/`62`). Common: i386\n`0x0003`, MIPS `0x0008`, PPC `0x0014`, PPC64 `0x0015`, s390 `0x0016`, ARM `0x0028`, x86-64 `0x003e`, AArch64 `0x00b7`,\nRISC-V `0x00f3`. Race probe answered from prebuilt `elf.py` (~13 s, first submit). Timed: synthesis dispatch missing\nagain -> `solver_incomplete` -> generalize ported D18's branch -> CORRECT.\n\n**Day 20 — Universal Appeal** (`macho.cpu_type_set`, kind `json` \"compact valid JSON array with exact values and\norder\", norm `trim`, id `d20-macho-001-macho-cpu-type-set`). Prompt: \"A macOS deployment includes thin and universal\nbinaries mixed with archives. Enumerate every CPU type and identify what truly supports the advertised fleet.\"\n(universal / archives / advertised fleet -- NOT asked).\n- Artifact: zip -> `macos-001.bin`, 56 B: a header-only THIN Mach-O -- `cffaedfe` MH_MAGIC_64 LE, cputype\n  `0c 00 00 01` = 0x0100000c (CPU_TYPE_ARM64 = ARM 12 | ABI64 0x01000000), cpusubtype 0 (ARM64_ALL), filetype 2\n  (MH_EXECUTE), ncmds 1, sizeofcmds 24, one LC_UUID (0x1b). Same bytes in single, TT and all 5 Mastery sets.\n- Key insight: the title pun (\"universal\" = fat binary) sets up a SET field -- one cputype per fat_arch slice -- but the\n  sample was thin, so the set has one element. Spelling = raw struct value like D9/D19: `\"0x%08x\"` of the u32 cputype,\n  ABI64 bit included -> `[\"0x0100000c\"]`. `[\"arm64\"]` (lipo/`file` name) was REJECTED.\n- Tools: `xxd -l 32 f` (cputype @4 LE for `cffaedfe`); `rabin2 -I` / `lief` for orientation. Prebuilt `lib.meta` fmt\n  `macho` HAD the extractor but `cpu_type_set` matched its scalar `cpu_type` branch -> a bare `0x0100000c`, not a list;\n  the worker wrapped it. Fat path (`fat_arch_cputypes`, fat_arch order) is unverified by the GM (order/dedupe unknown).\n- Single: wrong `[\"arm64\"]` at +34 s, CORRECT `[\"0x0100000c\"]` at +39 s. TT (25 fields) and Mastery (125) CORRECT\n  in-window FIRST try -- the D19 synthesis dispatch was carried over in the solver (no generalize needed).\n\n\"\"\"+s[old_end:]\n# conventions\nrep(\"\"\"  `0x00065bd0`. Width from the STRUCT / the\n  `_uNN_` in the id;\"\"\",\"\"\"  `0x00065bd0`. Width from the STRUCT / the\n  `_uNN_` in the id;\"\"\") if False else None\nrep(\"\"\"- Header integers as hex (`*_hex`): `0x` + lowercase hex ZERO-PADDED to the struct field's width: u16 PE Machine\n  `0x014c`, u16 ELF e_machine `0x003e` (D19), u32 AddressOfEntryPoint `0x00065bd0`.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- Header integers as hex (`*_hex`): `0x` + lowercase hex ZERO-PADDED to the struct field's width: u16 PE Machine\n  `0x014c`, u16 ELF e_machine `0x003e` (D19), u32 AddressOfEntryPoint `0x00065bd0`, u32 Mach-O cputype `0x0100000c`\n  (D20, inside a JSON list, even without `_hex` in the id; ABI64 bit kept, no name).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  - `*-synthesis-<algo>-order`: member names ordered by hex digest ascending (D15-D19 TT/Mastery; `case_insensitive`).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"  - `*-synthesis-<algo>-order`: member names ordered by hex digest ascending (D15-D20 TT/Mastery; `case_insensitive`).\n  - `macho.cpu_type_set`: `[\"0x%08x\", ...]` one per slice; thin = one element (D20). Fat: fat_arch order (unverified).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- Rejected spellings: `0x65bd0` (D10, unpadded); brace-less MSI GUID (D13); rels-file-order target list (D15);\n  bracket-less Message-ID (D16).\"\"\",\"\"\"- Rejected spellings: `0x65bd0` (D10, unpadded); brace-less MSI GUID (D13); rels-file-order target list (D15);\n  bracket-less Message-ID (D16); `[\"arm64\"]` arch name for `macho.cpu_type_set` (D20).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  (`ei_data`, `e_type`) have no GM spelling yet -- lib emits `ELFDATA2LSB` / `2`; prefer the `_hex` form if offered.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"  (`ei_data`, `e_type`) have no GM spelling yet -- lib emits `ELFDATA2LSB` / `2`; prefer the `_hex` form if offered.\n  D20 extends it: header CODES (machine, cputype, subtype, filetype) are emitted as raw `0x` hex, never as tool names.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  (most days, all of D15-19): ONE download\"\"\",\"\"\"  (most days, all of D15-20): ONE download\"\"\")\n# pitfalls\nrep(\"\"\"- Field suffix picks the spelling: `_u16_hex` = the raw struct value (D9: not `i386`/GOARCH; D19: not `x86-64`);\n  `_codec_name` = the tool vocabulary (D17: `pcm_s16le`, not the raw format tag `1` nor mediainfo's `PCM`).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- Field suffix picks the spelling: `_u16_hex` = the raw struct value (D9: not `i386`/GOARCH; D19: not `x86-64`);\n  `_codec_name` = the tool vocabulary (D17: `pcm_s16le`, not the raw format tag `1` nor mediainfo's `PCM`). NO suffix\n  on a binary-header code (D20 `cpu_type_set`, 1 wrong + 5 s): still the raw struct hex (`0x0100000c`), not `arm64`.\n  Only a field that SAYS `_name`/`_arch_names` gets a name.\n- Registry substring match (D20): prebuilt `macho` answered `cpu_type_set` through its scalar `cpu_type` branch -> a bare\n  hex string where the contract wants a JSON list. When answer_format is `json`, check the registry value is a list;\n  `_set`/`_list`/`_names` = one entry per item (per fat slice / per member), wrap a scalar thin-file value in `[...]`.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- Endianness (D19 pun): never `struct.unpack('<H')` an ELF/Mach-O field blindly -- EI_DATA (ELF @5) / the Mach-O magic\n  byte order decide; ELF32 vs ELF64 moves every offset after e_version (e_entry/e_phoff/e_shoff widths).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- Endianness (D19 pun): never `struct.unpack('<H')` an ELF/Mach-O field blindly -- EI_DATA (ELF @5) / the Mach-O magic\n  byte order decide (`cffaedfe` = LE; fat headers are ALWAYS BE, their slices carry their own magic); ELF32 vs ELF64\n  moves every offset after e_version. Fat: cputype is in BOTH fat_arch and the slice header -- they may disagree in a\n  variant (\"what truly supports\"): the set field reads fat_arch; note the slice header if they differ.\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPYEOF\nwc -l reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9758,"cache_read_input_tokens":83908,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9758},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"477ba029-865b-464a-9dbb-2d2f93cfd02a","uuid":"406d0440-8d1f-425d-b3a9-0c7a40e54b7b","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:18:16.299Z","request_id":"req_011CgDZ3k5X5Hz2Jc1bgCa4X","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01BK8uo1B6kWLHPTvSscCaMf":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'PYEOF'\np='reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md'\ns=open(p).read()\