`[\"0x%08x\", ...]` one per slice; thin = one element (D20). Fat: fat_arch order (unverified).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- Rejected spellings: `0x65bd0` (D10, unpadded); brace-less MSI GUID (D13); rels-file-order target list (D15);\n  bracket-less Message-ID (D16).\"\"\",\"\"\"- Rejected spellings: `0x65bd0` (D10, unpadded); brace-less MSI GUID (D13); rels-file-order target list (D15);\n  bracket-less Message-ID (D16); `[\"arm64\"]` arch name for `macho.cpu_type_set` (D20).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  (`ei_data`, `e_type`) have no GM spelling yet -- lib emits `ELFDATA2LSB` / `2`; prefer the `_hex` form if offered.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"  (`ei_data`, `e_type`) have no GM spelling yet -- lib emits `ELFDATA2LSB` / `2`; prefer the `_hex` form if offered.\n  D20 extends it: header CODES (machine, cputype, subtype, filetype) are emitted as raw `0x` hex, never as tool names.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  (most days, all of D15-19): ONE download\"\"\",\"\"\"  (most days, all of D15-20): ONE download\"\"\")\n# pitfalls\nrep(\"\"\"- Field suffix picks the spelling: `_u16_hex` = the raw struct value (D9: not `i386`/GOARCH; D19: not `x86-64`);\n  `_codec_name` = the tool vocabulary (D17: `pcm_s16le`, not the raw format tag `1` nor mediainfo's `PCM`).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- Field suffix picks the spelling: `_u16_hex` = the raw struct value (D9: not `i386`/GOARCH; D19: not `x86-64`);\n  `_codec_name` = the tool vocabulary (D17: `pcm_s16le`, not the raw format tag `1` nor mediainfo's `PCM`). NO suffix\n  on a binary-header code (D20 `cpu_type_set`, 1 wrong + 5 s): still the raw struct hex (`0x0100000c`), not `arm64`.\n  Only a field that SAYS `_name`/`_arch_names` gets a name.\n- Registry substring match (D20): prebuilt `macho` answered `cpu_type_set` through its scalar `cpu_type` branch -> a bare\n  hex string where the contract wants a JSON list. When answer_format is `json`, check the registry value is a list;\n  `_set`/`_list`/`_names` = one entry per item (per fat slice / per member), wrap a scalar thin-file value in `[...]`.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- Endianness (D19 pun): never `struct.unpack('<H')` an ELF/Mach-O field blindly -- EI_DATA (ELF @5) / the Mach-O magic\n  byte order decide; ELF32 vs ELF64 moves every offset after e_version (e_entry/e_phoff/e_shoff widths).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- Endianness (D19 pun): never `struct.unpack('<H')` an ELF/Mach-O field blindly -- EI_DATA (ELF @5) / the Mach-O magic\n  byte order decide (`cffaedfe` = LE; fat headers are ALWAYS BE, their slices carry their own magic); ELF32 vs ELF64\n  moves every offset after e_version. Fat: cputype is in BOTH fat_arch and the slice header -- they may disagree in a\n  variant (\"what truly supports\"): the set field reads fat_arch; note the slice header if they differ.\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPYEOF\nwc -l reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md"}}}
