next \"fleet\"/bytecode family |\n\"\"\"\nanchor = s.index(\"| 121 | ELF special objects\")\neol = s.index(\"\\n\", anchor)+1\ns = s[:eol]+newrows+s[eol:]\nrep(\"\"\"cf fa ed fe / ce fa ed fe / ca fe ba be  Mach-O / fat (cafebabe + major@6 >= 45 = Java class)   struct; rabin2 -I; lief\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"cf fa ed fe/ce fa ed fe LE (fe ed fa cf BE) Mach-O cputype u32@4 (D20 `[\"0x0100000c\"]` arm64, list of 0x%08x per slice, NOT `arm64`); fat ca fe ba be/bf BE nfat@4, 20/32-B fat_arch; nfat>=45 = Java class\"\"\")\n# gaps JSON\na=s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\")\nj0=s.index(\"```json\",a)+len(\"```json\"); j1=s.index(\"```\",j0)\ngaps=json.loads(s[j0:j1])\ngaps=[g for g in gaps if g[\"id\"]!=\"macho-header\"]\nbyid={g[\"id\"]:g for g in gaps}\nfor k in (\"elf-dynamic-notes\",\"elf-ident-hex-siblings\",\"elf-arch-synthesis\"):\n    byid[k][\"priority\"]=2\nbyid[\"macho-codesign-dylibs\"][\"priority\"]=1\nbyid[\"linux-packages\"][\"priority\"]=2\nbyid[\"bplist-macos\"][\"priority\"]=2\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"macho-fat-slice-sets\",\"concept\":\"Mach-O universal/fat per-slice SET fields (cputype/cpusubtype sets, slice table, fat_arch vs slice-header mismatch)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D20 GM field `macho.cpu_type_set` = compact JSON list of `\\\"0x%08x\\\"` cputypes (thin -> one element `[\\\"0x0100000c\\\"]`, GM-confirmed; name `arm64` REJECTED). Prebuilt macho.py answers `cpu_type_set` via its scalar `cpu_type` branch (bare string) -- fix in a NEW module lib/meta/prebuilt/macho_sets.py registering fmt macho (aliases mach_o, macos, universal) fields that return LISTS: cpu_type_set / cputype_set / cpu_types (fat: fat_arch order, keep duplicates out? -> emit fat_arch order, dedupe preserving first occurrence; thin: [header cputype]), cpu_subtype_set (`0x%08x` of the RAW cpusubtype incl. capability bits 0x80000000 for arm64e; also cpu_subtype_masked_set with & 0x00ffffff), slice_count / fat_nfat_arch (thin -> 1? no: thin -> `none` for fat_*; slice_count thin -> 1), fat_arch_offsets_hex / fat_arch_sizes / fat_arch_aligns (2^align), slice_header_cputype_set (cputype read from each slice's own Mach-O header at offset), fat_slice_mismatch (true if any fat_arch cputype != slice header cputype; also mismatched_slice_indexes JSON), fat_magic_u32_hex (`0xcafebabe` / `0xcafebabf` fat64: 32-B fat_arch_64 with u64 offset/size), filetype_set, is_universal (`true`/`false`). Fat headers are ALWAYS big-endian; slices carry their own magic (LE `cffaedfe`/`cefaedfe`, BE `feedfacf`/`feedface`). Disambiguate Java class: `cafebabe` with u32 @4 >= 45 (or u16 major @6 >= 45 and @4 u16 minor small) -> not fat -> `none`. Non-Mach-O (ELF/PE/text) -> `none`. Test on synthesized thin arm64, thin x86_64 (0x01000007), fat x86_64+arm64, fat64, a fat whose slice header disagrees, and a Java class.\"},\n {\"id\":\"macho-arch-name-vocab\",\"concept\":\"Architecture NAME spellings for Mach-O / ELF / PE when a field explicitly asks for names\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Only used when the field id says `_name`/`_names`/`_arch`/`_archs`/`architectures` (D20 proved codes default to hex). fmt macho: arch_names / arch_name_set (lipo/`file` vocabulary: 7 i386, 0x01000007 x86_64 (subtype 8 -> x86_64h), 12 arm (subtype 9 armv7, 11 armv7s, 6 armv6, 16? armv7k=12), 0x0100000c arm64 (subtype 2 -> arm64e), 0x0200000c arm64_32, 18 ppc, 0x01000012 ppc64), cputype_constant_name (CPU_TYPE_ARM64 ...), filetype_name (MH_EXECUTE/MH_DYLIB/MH_BUNDLE/MH_OBJECT/MH_DYLINKER/MH_KEXT_BUNDLE/MH_DSYM), platform_name from LC_BUILD_VERSION (1 macos, 2 ios, 3 tvos, 4 watchos, 5 bridgeos, 6 maccatalyst, 7 iossimulator, 11 visionos). fmt elf: e_machine_name (readelf strings `Advanced Micro Devices X86-64`, short `x86_64`/`aarch64`), e_machine_constant (EM_X86_64). fmt pe: coff_machine_name (IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_AMD64 / short `x64`/`ARM64`/`x86`). Emit the short lipo/uname-style name for `*_name(s)` and the constant for `*_constant`. Never registered under a `_hex` field.\"},\n {\"id\":\"ar-static-archives\",\"concept\":\"Unix `ar` archives (.a static libs, universal .a, Windows .lib) members and object architectures\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D20 flavor 'thin and universal binaries mixed with archives'. fmt ar (aliases archive, static_lib, a, lib): magic `!<arch>\\\\n` @0 (also thin `!<thin>\\\\n`); 60-B headers: name[16] date[12] uid[6] gid[6] mode[8 octal] size[10] fmag `` `\\\\n `` ; data padded to even. Names: BSD `#1/<len>` (name follows header, counted in size), GNU `/` = symbol table, `//` = long-name table, `/<off>` reference, trailing `/` stripped; BSD symtab `__.SYMDEF`/`__.SYMDEF SORTED`. Fields: member_names (JSON, archive order, symbol/longname tables EXCLUDED), member_count, symbol_table_present, symbol_names (GNU: u32 BE count + offsets + NUL strings; BSD ranlib structs LE), member_mtimes_utc (ISO-8601 Z from decimal epoch), member_sizes, member_modes (octal string), member_cpu_type_set (Mach-O object members -> `0x%08x` list, dedupe, archive order), member_e_machine_set (ELF objects -> `0x%04x`), member_coff_machine_set (COFF .obj in .lib -> `0x%04x`). A universal static lib is a FAT wrapper whose slices are ar archives: route `cafebabe` -> slice -> `!<arch>`. Non-ar -> `none`.\"},\n {\"id\":\"macos-xar-pkg-dmg\",\"concept\":\"macOS installer containers: xar `.pkg`, flat-package TOC, DMG koly trailer\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt pkg (aliases xar, macos_pkg): header `xar!` (78 61 72 21) BE: header_size u16 @4, version u16 @6, toc_length_compressed u64 @8, toc_length_uncompressed u64 @16, cksum_alg u32 @24 (0 none, 1 sha1, 2 md5, 3 other + name); TOC = zlib XML after the header. Fields: xar_version, toc_checksum_alg (`sha1`/`md5`/`none`), file_names (TOC <file><name> paths joined with `/`, TOC order JSON), file_count, distribution_host_architectures (Distribution XML `<options hostArchitectures=\\\"x86_64,arm64\\\"/>` -> JSON list in stored order), distribution_min_os (`<allowed-os-versions><os-version min=>`), package_identifiers (PackageInfo `<pkg-info identifier= version=>`), package_versions, signature_present (TOC <signature>), signer_cert_cn (x509 in TOC KeyInfo, worker-only if cryptography not allowed). Heap files (Distribution, PackageInfo) at heap offset = header_size + toc_compressed + <data><offset>, encoding gzip/bzip2/none -- only zlib/bz2 stdlib. fmt dmg: `koly` trailer in LAST 512 B (BE): version u32 @4, header_size @8, flags @12, data_fork_offset u64 @24, data_fork_length @32, xml_offset u64 @216, xml_length @224, image_variant u32 @0x1E8, sector_count u64 @0x1EC; fields koly_version, data_fork_length, xml_plist_partition_names (plist blkx Name list), sector_count. Non-matching -> `none`.\"},\n {\"id\":\"macos-app-bundle-plist\",\"concept\":\"Zipped `.app` / `.framework` bundles: Info.plist advertised architectures and minimum OS vs the real binary\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D20 'identify what truly supports the advertised fleet'. fmt app (aliases app_bundle, bundle, macos_app; also plist fields under fmt plist): inside a zip (or the asked member is the Info.plist itself) find `*.app/Contents/Info.plist` (macOS) or `*.app/Info.plist` (iOS); parse XML or `bplist00` with stdlib plistlib.loads(bytes). Fields: bundle_identifier (CFBundleIdentifier), bundle_executable, bundle_short_version (CFBundleShortVersionString), bundle_version (CFBundleVersion), minimum_system_version (LSMinimumSystemVersion verbatim), architecture_priority (LSArchitecturePriority JSON list stored order), requires_native_execution (LSRequiresNativeExecution bool -> true/false), supported_platforms (CFBundleSupportedPlatforms JSON), executable_cpu_type_set (Contents/MacOS/<CFBundleExecutable> Mach-O -> `0x%08x` list, fat_arch order), executable_min_os (LC_BUILD_VERSION minos X.Y.Z / LC_VERSION_MIN_MACOSX), advertised_vs_actual_mismatch (true if an LSArchitecturePriority arch is missing from the executable's slices; arch names mapped arm64->0x0100000c, x86_64->0x01000007, i386->7, arm64e->0x0100000c/subtype 2). Values verbatim; booleans `true`/`false`.\"},\n {\"id\":\"macho-fleet-synthesis\",\"concept\":\"Cross-file architecture-support synthesis over Mach-O / fat / ar / ELF / PE members\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Extend lib.meta.synthesis (fmt synthesis) for ids `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<key>` over the question's `Files: [...]` list (parse like digest_order; get_bytes per set): files_supporting_<arch> / arch_support_files (names whose Mach-O fat_arch/thin cputype, ELF e_machine or PE Machine covers the asked arch: arm64 = Mach-O 0x0100000c / ELF 0x00b7 / PE 0xaa64; x86_64 = 0x01000007 / 0x003e / 0x8664; i386 = 7 / 0x0003 / 0x014c) in Files order unless 'sorted'/'ascending' is said, universal_files (fat with >= 2 distinct cputypes), thin_files, cpu_type_groups (JSON object `0x%08x` -> sorted names), extension_or_name_liars (name says universal/fat/x86_64/arm64 but slices disagree), union_cpu_type_set (sorted? -> emit first-seen order), count_<arch>. Archives (`!<arch>`, zip) expand to their object members. Compact JSON; descending only if stated.\"},\n {\"id\":\"msix-appx-arch\",\"concept\":\"MSIX/AppX packages and bundles: Identity incl. ProcessorArchitecture, bundle package list\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Windows-side 'fleet' analog. fmt msix (aliases appx, appxbundle, msixbundle): zip with `AppxManifest.xml` (or `AppxMetadata/AppxBundleManifest.xml`); xml.etree local-name. Fields: identity_name, identity_publisher, identity_version, identity_processor_architecture (`x64`/`x86`/`arm64`/`neutral` verbatim), target_device_families (JSON `Name MinVersion` stored order), bundle_package_architectures (JSON per <Package Architecture=> stored order), bundle_package_file_names, executable (Applications/Application@Executable), capabilities (JSON names stored order), signature_present (`AppxSignature.p7x`), block_map_hash_method (AppxBlockMap.xml HashMethod). Non-package -> `none`.\"},\n {\"id\":\"cpio-payloads\",\"concept\":\"cpio archives (newc/odc/binary) and Apple pbzx payloads\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt cpio (aliases payload, initramfs): newc `070701`/crc `070702` (110-B ASCII-hex header: ino mode uid gid nlink mtime filesize devmajor devminor rdevmajor rdevminor namesize check; name + data 4-byte aligned), odc `070707` (76-B octal), binary `c7 71`/`71 c7` (26-B, endian by magic); stop at `TRAILER!!!`. Fields: format (`newc`/`crc`/`odc`/`bin`), member_names (archive order, `TRAILER!!!` excluded), member_count, member_modes (octal string `0100755`), member_mtimes_utc, member_sizes, member_cpu_type_set / member_e_machine_set for embedded binaries. pbzx (`pbzx` magic, u64 BE flags then chunks of u64 decompressed/compressed size + XZ data) -> lzma.decompress chunks -> cpio. gzip/xz-wrapped cpio: decompress first. Non-cpio -> `none`.\"},\n {\"id\":\"jar-manifest-class-versions\",\"concept\":\"JAR/WAR packaging: MANIFEST.MF attributes and the class-file version set\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt jar (aliases java_archive, war, ear; manifest fields also under fmt java): zip with `META-INF/MANIFEST.MF`; parse RFC-822-like manifest (72-byte lines, continuation = leading single space; main section until blank line). Fields: manifest_main_class, manifest_created_by, manifest_version, manifest_multi_release (`true`/`false`), implementation_title/version/vendor, automatic_module_name, class_path (JSON split on spaces), class_major_version_set (JSON sorted ascending ints of every `*.class` member's u16 BE major @6, incl. META-INF/versions/N/), max_class_major_version, java_version_min (major-44: 52 -> 8, 55 -> 11, 61 -> 17, 65 -> 21), signature_files (META-INF/*.SF/*.RSA/*.DSA/*.EC names), class_count. Non-jar -> `none`.\"}\n]\nids={g[\"id\"] for g in gaps}\nfor n in new: assert n[\"id\"] not in ids\n# insert new after the p1 synthesis items\ngaps = new[:6] + gaps + new[6:]\ngaps.sort(key=lambda g: g[\"priority\"])   # stable\nbody=\"\\n\"+\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in gaps)+\"\\n]\\n\"\ns=s[:j0]+body+s[j1:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPYEOF\ngrep -n 'Ranking (D19' reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1439,"cache_read_input_tokens":108782,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1439},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"477ba029-865b-464a-9dbb-2d2f93cfd02a","uuid":"2492ec0a-d876-4605-ae14-49c6e99d59ad","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:20:16.506Z","request_id":"req_011CgDZBDnbN7gaFumjyAkEF","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XM6cGKajiHXDwKQQn1AVz5":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\np='reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(old,new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)==1, old[:80]\n    s=s.replace(old,new)\nrep(\"# metadata-forensics — coverage atlas (as of D19 post-run, 2026-10-19)\",\n    \"# metadata-forensics — coverage atlas (as of D20 post-run, 2026-10-20)\")\nrep(\"\"\"groups\"), then Mach-O (fat/thin, LC_UUID, codesign) or Linux packaging (deb/rpm/AppImage) as the next family.\n\"\"\",\"\"\"groups\"), then Mach-O (fat/thin, LC_UUID, codesign) or Linux packaging (deb/rpm/AppImage) as the next family.\n**D20 \"Universal Appeal\" = Mach-O** (`macho.cpu_type_set` of one `macos-001.bin` -> `[\"0x0100000c\"]`; id\n`d20-macho-001-macho-...`: plain fmt `macho`). ELF stayed ONE day (like audio/video), so the lane is walking executable\nFORMATS one header field each: PE (D9) -> ELF (D19) -> Mach-O (D20). Artifact = a 56-B THIN arm64 header (MH_MAGIC_64\nLE + LC_UUID), identical in every mode/set. GM spelling = raw u32 struct hex inside a JSON list, even without `_hex` in\nthe id; the name `[\"arm64\"]` was REJECTED. First SET-valued header field (one entry per fat slice). Flavor: \"A macOS\ndeployment includes thin and universal binaries mixed with archives. Enumerate every CPU type and identify what truly\nsupports the advertised fleet.\" (fat slices / archives / advertised-vs-actual -- not asked). D21-D23 most plausibly:\n(a) a deeper Mach-O field or a REAL fat binary (cputype set over fat_arch slices, cpusubtype incl. arm64e/x86_64h,\nfat_arch vs slice-header mismatch = \"what truly supports\"); (b) the \"archives\" side -- `ar` static libraries (`.a`,\nuniversal `.a` = fat of ar), macOS installers (xar `.pkg`, `.dmg` koly), zipped `.app` bundles with Info.plist\n(LSMinimumSystemVersion / LSArchitecturePriority = the \"advertised fleet\"); (c) an arch/fleet synthesis across Mach-O +\nELF + PE (which members run on arm64); (d) the next family after the executable trio: Java/JAR/class, WASM, APK/DEX\n(mobile overlap), MSIX/AppX (Windows packaging with ProcessorArchitecture), cpio payloads, firmware.\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| 83 | Mach-O thin/fat: cputype, filetype, ncmds, flags, LC_UUID, min OS / build version | prebuilt macho |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| 83 | Mach-O thin/fat: cputype, filetype, ncmds, flags, LC_UUID, min OS / build version | seen D20 `macho.cpu_type_set` (`[\"0x0100000c\"]`: JSON list of `0x%08x` per slice, thin = 1; name `arm64` REJECTED); rest prebuilt macho (registry answered `cpu_type_set` as a SCALAR -- list shape = gap macho-fat-slice-sets) |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| 119 | Mach-O deeper: LC_LOAD_DYLIB list, LC_RPATH, LC_MAIN entryoff, segment names, code signature CodeDirectory identifier/teamID/cdhash, entitlements | gap (macho-codesign-dylibs; header fields prebuilt macho) |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| 119 | Mach-O deeper: LC_LOAD_DYLIB list, LC_RPATH, LC_MAIN entryoff, segment names, code signature CodeDirectory identifier/teamID/cdhash, entitlements | prebuilt macho_lc (macho-codesign-dylibs; spellings unverified) |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| 73 | MSIX/AppX: AppxManifest Identity Name/Publisher/Version, signature | gap |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| 73 | MSIX/AppX: AppxManifest Identity Name/Publisher/Version/ProcessorArchitecture, bundles, signature | gap (msix-appx-arch) |\"\"\")\nnewrows=\"\"\"| 122 | Mach-O fat/universal SETS: cputype + cpusubtype per fat_arch (fat `cafebabe` / fat64 `cafebabf`), slice offsets/sizes/align, slice-header vs fat_arch mismatch, arm64e (subtype 2, caps bits 0x80000000 masked?), x86_64h (8) | gap (macho-fat-slice-sets) | `ca fe ba be` + nfat_arch small (< 45, else Java class) | struct (BE fat headers); `lipo -detailed_info` (M); `rabin2 -A` (I) | high -- D20 pun not exercised yet |\n| 123 | Arch NAME vocabularies across formats (Mach-O `arm64`/`x86_64`/`arm64e`/`i386`/`ppc`, ELF readelf names, PE `x64`/`ARM64`, Go GOARCH, Debian arch) | gap (macho-arch-name-vocab) | field ends `_name(s)` / `_arch(s)` | static maps in lib | med -- only when the id says name |\n| 124 | `ar` static archives (`.a`, `.lib`): member names (BSD `#1/NN`, GNU `//` + `/NN`), symbol table `__.SYMDEF`/`/`, member mtimes/uid/mode, per-member object cputype/e_machine | gap (ar-static-archives) | `!<arch>\\\\n` @0 (60-B headers ending `` `\\\\n ``) | struct; `ar t` (I) | high -- D20 \"mixed with archives\" |\n| 125 | macOS installers: xar `.pkg` (`xar!` header, zlib TOC XML: file names, PackageInfo identifier/version, Distribution `hostArchitectures`), DMG (`koly` trailer last 512 B), zipped `.app` Info.plist (CFBundleIdentifier, CFBundleShortVersionString, LSMinimumSystemVersion, LSArchitecturePriority) | gap (macos-xar-pkg-dmg, macos-app-bundle-plist) | `78 61 72 21`; `6b 6f 6c 79` @-512; zip `*.app/Contents/Info.plist` | struct + zlib + plistlib; `xar -tf` (M), `hdiutil` (M) | high-med -- \"macOS deployment ... archives\" |\n| 126 | Fleet / arch-support synthesis: which members support arch X, members whose name/extension claims `universal` but are thin, group-by cputype set, archive members' archs | gap (macho-fleet-synthesis) | synthesis text \"supports\", \"fleet\", \"universal\", \"architecture\" | lib.meta.synthesis + per-format machine extractors | med-high |\n| 127 | Payload archives: cpio newc/odc/bin (`070701`/`070707`/`c7 71`) member names/modes/mtimes, pbzx (`pbzx`) Apple payloads | gap (cpio-payloads) | `30 37 30 37 30 31`; `70 62 7a 78` | struct + lzma | low-med |\n| 128 | JAR / Java packaging: META-INF/MANIFEST.MF (Main-Class, Created-By, Multi-Release, Implementation-Version), class major-version SET across members | gap (jar-manifest-class-versions) | zip with `META-INF/MANIFEST.MF` + `*.class` (`cafebabe`) | zipfile + struct | med -- next \"fleet\"/bytecode family |\n\"\"\"\nanchor = s.index(\"| 121 | ELF special objects\")\neol = s.index(\"\\n\", anchor)+1\ns = s[:eol]+newrows+s[eol:]\nrep(\"\"\"cf fa ed fe / ce fa ed fe / ca fe ba be  Mach-O / fat (cafebabe + major@6 >= 45 = Java class)   struct; rabin2 -I; lief\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"cf fa ed fe/ce fa ed fe LE (fe ed fa cf BE) Mach-O cputype u32@4 (D20 `[\"0x0100000c\"]` arm64, list of 0x%08x per slice, NOT `arm64`); fat ca fe ba be/bf BE nfat@4, 20/32-B fat_arch; nfat>=45 = Java class\"\"\")\n# gaps JSON\na=s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\")\nj0=s.index(\"```json\",a)+len(\"```json\"); j1=s.index(\"```\",j0)\ngaps=json.loads(s[j0:j1])\ngaps=[g for g in gaps if g[\"id\"]!=\"macho-header\"]\nbyid={g[\"id\"]:g for g in gaps}\nfor k in (\"elf-dynamic-notes\",\"elf-ident-hex-siblings\",\"elf-arch-synthesis\"):\n    byid[k][\"priority\"]=2\nbyid[\"macho-codesign-dylibs\"][\"priority\"]=1\nbyid[\"linux-packages\"][\"priority\"]=2\nbyid[\"bplist-macos\"][\"priority\"]=2\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"macho-fat-slice-sets\",\"concept\":\"Mach-O universal/fat per-slice SET fields (cputype/cpusubtype sets, slice table, fat_arch vs slice-header mismatch)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D20 GM field `macho.cpu_type_set` = compact JSON list of `\\\"0x%08x\\\"` cputypes (thin -> one element `[\\\"0x0100000c\\\"]`, GM-confirmed; name `arm64` REJECTED). Prebuilt macho.py answers `cpu_type_set` via its scalar `cpu_type` branch (bare string) -- fix in a NEW module lib/meta/prebuilt/macho_sets.py registering fmt macho (aliases mach_o, macos, universal) fields that return LISTS: cpu_type_set / cputype_set / cpu_types (fat: fat_arch order, keep duplicates out? -> emit fat_arch order, dedupe preserving first occurrence; thin: [header cputype]), cpu_subtype_set (`0x%08x` of the RAW cpusubtype incl. capability bits 0x80000000 for arm64e; also cpu_subtype_masked_set with & 0x00ffffff), slice_count / fat_nfat_arch (thin -> 1? no: thin -> `none` for fat_*; slice_count thin -> 1), fat_arch_offsets_hex / fat_arch_sizes / fat_arch_aligns (2^align), slice_header_cputype_set (cputype read from each slice's own Mach-O header at offset), fat_slice_mismatch (true if any fat_arch cputype != slice header cputype; also mismatched_slice_indexes JSON), fat_magic_u32_hex (`0xcafebabe` / `0xcafebabf` fat64: 32-B fat_arch_64 with u64 offset/size), filetype_set, is_universal (`true`/`false`). Fat headers are ALWAYS big-endian; slices carry their own magic (LE `cffaedfe`/`cefaedfe`, BE `feedfacf`/`feedface`). Disambiguate Java class: `cafebabe` with u32 @4 >= 45 (or u16 major @6 >= 45 and @4 u16 minor small) -> not fat -> `none`. Non-Mach-O (ELF/PE/text) -> `none`. Test on synthesized thin arm64, thin x86_64 (0x01000007), fat x86_64+arm64, fat64, a fat whose slice header disagrees, and a Java class.\"},\n {\"id\":\"macho-arch-name-vocab\",\"concept\":\"Architecture NAME spellings for Mach-O / ELF / PE when a field explicitly asks for names\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Only used when the field id says `_name`/`_names`/`_arch`/`_archs`/`architectures` (D20 proved codes default to hex). fmt macho: arch_names / arch_name_set (lipo/`file` vocabulary: 7 i386, 0x01000007 x86_64 (subtype 8 -> x86_64h), 12 arm (subtype 9 armv7, 11 armv7s, 6 armv6, 16? armv7k=12), 0x0100000c arm64 (subtype 2 -> arm64e), 0x0200000c arm64_32, 18 ppc, 0x01000012 ppc64), cputype_constant_name (CPU_TYPE_ARM64 ...), filetype_name (MH_EXECUTE/MH_DYLIB/MH_BUNDLE/MH_OBJECT/MH_DYLINKER/MH_KEXT_BUNDLE/MH_DSYM), platform_name from LC_BUILD_VERSION (1 macos, 2 ios, 3 tvos, 4 watchos, 5 bridgeos, 6 maccatalyst, 7 iossimulator, 11 visionos). fmt elf: e_machine_name (readelf strings `Advanced Micro Devices X86-64`, short `x86_64`/`aarch64`), e_machine_constant (EM_X86_64). fmt pe: coff_machine_name (IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_AMD64 / short `x64`/`ARM64`/`x86`). Emit the short lipo/uname-style name for `*_name(s)` and the constant for `*_constant`. Never registered under a `_hex` field.\"},\n {\"id\":\"ar-static-archives\",\"concept\":\"Unix `ar` archives (.a static libs, universal .a, Windows .lib) members and object architectures\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D20 flavor 'thin and universal binaries mixed with archives'. fmt ar (aliases archive, static_lib, a, lib): magic `!<arch>\\\\n` @0 (also thin `!<thin>\\\\n`); 60-B headers: name[16] date[12] uid[6] gid[6] mode[8 octal] size[10] fmag `` `\\\\n `` ; data padded to even. Names: BSD `#1/<len>` (name follows header, counted in size), GNU `/` = symbol table, `//` = long-name table, `/<off>` reference, trailing `/` stripped; BSD symtab `__.SYMDEF`/`__.SYMDEF SORTED`. Fields: member_names (JSON, archive order, symbol/longname tables EXCLUDED), member_count, symbol_table_present, symbol_names (GNU: u32 BE count + offsets + NUL strings; BSD ranlib structs LE), member_mtimes_utc (ISO-8601 Z from decimal epoch), member_sizes, member_modes (octal string), member_cpu_type_set (Mach-O object members -> `0x%08x` list, dedupe, archive order), member_e_machine_set (ELF objects -> `0x%04x`), member_coff_machine_set (COFF .obj in .lib -> `0x%04x`). A universal static lib is a FAT wrapper whose slices are ar archives: route `cafebabe` -> slice -> `!<arch>`. Non-ar -> `none`.\"},\n {\"id\":\"macos-xar-pkg-dmg\",\"concept\":\"macOS installer containers: xar `.pkg`, flat-package TOC, DMG koly trailer\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt pkg (aliases xar, macos_pkg): header `xar!` (78 61 72 21) BE: header_size u16 @4, version u16 @6, toc_length_compressed u64 @8, toc_length_uncompressed u64 @16, cksum_alg u32 @24 (0 none, 1 sha1, 2 md5, 3 other + name); TOC = zlib XML after the header. Fields: xar_version, toc_checksum_alg (`sha1`/`md5`/`none`), file_names (TOC <file><name> paths joined with `/`, TOC order JSON), file_count, distribution_host_architectures (Distribution XML `<options hostArchitectures=\\\"x86_64,arm64\\\"/>` -> JSON list in stored order), distribution_min_os (`<allowed-os-versions><os-version min=>`), package_identifiers (PackageInfo `<pkg-info identifier= version=>`), package_versions, signature_present (TOC <signature>), signer_cert_cn (x509 in TOC KeyInfo, worker-only if cryptography not allowed). Heap files (Distribution, PackageInfo) at heap offset = header_size + toc_compressed + <data><offset>, encoding gzip/bzip2/none -- only zlib/bz2 stdlib. fmt dmg: `koly` trailer in LAST 512 B (BE): version u32 @4, header_size @8, flags @12, data_fork_offset u64 @24, data_fork_length @32, xml_offset u64 @216, xml_length @224, image_variant u32 @0x1E8, sector_count u64 @0x1EC; fields koly_version, data_fork_length, xml_plist_partition_names (plist blkx Name list), sector_count. Non-matching -> `none`.\"},\n {\"id\":\"macos-app-bundle-plist\",\"concept\":\"Zipped `.app` / `.framework` bundles: Info.plist advertised architectures and minimum OS vs the real binary\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D20 'identify what truly supports the advertised fleet'. fmt app (aliases app_bundle, bundle, macos_app; also plist fields under fmt plist): inside a zip (or the asked member is the Info.plist itself) find `*.app/Contents/Info.plist` (macOS) or `*.app/Info.plist` (iOS); parse XML or `bplist00` with stdlib plistlib.loads(bytes). Fields: bundle_identifier (CFBundleIdentifier), bundle_executable, bundle_short_version (CFBundleShortVersionString), bundle_version (CFBundleVersion), minimum_system_version (LSMinimumSystemVersion verbatim), architecture_priority (LSArchitecturePriority JSON list stored order), requires_native_execution (LSRequiresNativeExecution bool -> true/false), supported_platforms (CFBundleSupportedPlatforms JSON), executable_cpu_type_set (Contents/MacOS/<CFBundleExecutable> Mach-O -> `0x%08x` list, fat_arch order), executable_min_os (LC_BUILD_VERSION minos X.Y.Z / LC_VERSION_MIN_MACOSX), advertised_vs_actual_mismatch (true if an LSArchitecturePriority arch is missing from the executable's slices; arch names mapped arm64->0x0100000c, x86_64->0x01000007, i386->7, arm64e->0x0100000c/subtype 2). Values verbatim; booleans `true`/`false`.\"},\n {\"id\":\"macho-fleet-synthesis\",\"concept\":\"Cross-file architecture-support synthesis over Mach-O / fat / ar / ELF / PE members\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Extend lib.meta.synthesis (fmt synthesis) for ids `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<key>` over the question's `Files: [...]` list (parse like digest_order; get_bytes per set): files_supporting_<arch> / arch_support_files (names whose Mach-O fat_arch/thin cputype, ELF e_machine or PE Machine covers the asked arch: arm64 = Mach-O 0x0100000c / ELF 0x00b7 / PE 0xaa64; x86_64 = 0x01000007 / 0x003e / 0x8664; i386 = 7 / 0x0003 / 0x014c) in Files order unless 'sorted'/'ascending' is said, universal_files (fat with >= 2 distinct cputypes), thin_files, cpu_type_groups (JSON object `0x%08x` -> sorted names), extension_or_name_liars (name says universal/fat/x86_64/arm64 but slices disagree), union_cpu_type_set (sorted? -> emit first-seen order), count_<arch>. Archives (`!<arch>`, zip) expand to their object members. Compact JSON; descending only if stated.\"},\n {\"id\":\"msix-appx-arch\",\"concept\":\"MSIX/AppX packages and bundles: Identity incl. ProcessorArchitecture, bundle package list\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Windows-side 'fleet' analog. fmt msix (aliases appx, appxbundle, msixbundle): zip with `AppxManifest.xml` (or `AppxMetadata/AppxBundleManifest.xml`); xml.etree local-name. Fields: identity_name, identity_publisher, identity_version, identity_processor_architecture (`x64`/`x86`/`arm64`/`neutral` verbatim), target_device_families (JSON `Name MinVersion` stored order), bundle_package_architectures (JSON per <Package Architecture=> stored order), bundle_package_file_names, executable (Applications/Application@Executable), capabilities (JSON names stored order), signature_present (`AppxSignature.p7x`), block_map_hash_method (AppxBlockMap.xml HashMethod). Non-package -> `none`.\"},\n {\"id\":\"cpio-payloads\",\"concept\":\"cpio archives (newc/odc/binary) and Apple pbzx payloads\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt cpio (aliases payload, initramfs): newc `070701`/crc `070702` (110-B ASCII-hex header: ino mode uid gid nlink mtime filesize devmajor devminor rdevmajor rdevminor namesize check; name + data 4-byte aligned), odc `070707` (76-B octal), binary `c7 71`/`71 c7` (26-B, endian by magic); stop at `TRAILER!!!`. Fields: format (`newc`/`crc`/`odc`/`bin`), member_names (archive order, `TRAILER!!!` excluded), member_count, member_modes (octal string `0100755`), member_mtimes_utc, member_sizes, member_cpu_type_set / member_e_machine_set for embedded binaries. pbzx (`pbzx` magic, u64 BE flags then chunks of u64 decompressed/compressed size + XZ data) -> lzma.decompress chunks -> cpio. gzip/xz-wrapped cpio: decompress first. Non-cpio -> `none`.\"},\n {\"id\":\"jar-manifest-class-versions\",\"concept\":\"JAR/WAR packaging: MANIFEST.MF attributes and the class-file version set\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt jar (aliases java_archive, war, ear; manifest fields also under fmt java): zip with `META-INF/MANIFEST.MF`; parse RFC-822-like manifest (72-byte lines, continuation = leading single space; main section until blank line). Fields: manifest_main_class, manifest_created_by, manifest_version, manifest_multi_release (`true`/`false`), implementation_title/version/vendor, automatic_module_name, class_path (JSON split on spaces), class_major_version_set (JSON sorted ascending ints of every `*.class` member's u16 BE major @6, incl. META-INF/versions/N/), max_class_major_version, java_version_min (major-44: 52 -> 8, 55 -> 11, 61 -> 17, 65 -> 21), signature_files (META-INF/*.SF/*.RSA/*.DSA/*.EC names), class_count. Non-jar -> `none`.\"}\n]\nids={g[\"id\"] for g in gaps}\nfor n in new: assert n[\"id\"] not in ids\n# insert new after the p1 synthesis items\ngaps = new[:6] + gaps + new[6:]\ngaps.sort(key=lambda g: g[\"priority\"])   # stable\nbody=\"\\n\"+\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in gaps)+\"\\n]\\n\"\ns=s[:j0]+body+s[j1:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPYEOF\ngrep -n 'Ranking (D19' reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md"}}}
