{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDZJpTcNRPRytYPEwXTw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I updated both metadata-forensics files and touched nothing else.\n\n- **`reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md`** (now 229 lines): new Day 20 entry for \"Universal Appeal\". The question asked for `macho.cpu_type_set`. The artifact was a 56-byte thin arm64 Mach-O header, not a universal one. The GM accepted `[\"0x0100000c\"]` (raw 8-digit hex, one entry per slice) and rejected the name `[\"arm64\"]`. The single solve lost that one submit and was CORRECT at about 39 s. Time Trial and Mastery passed in-window on the first try. I also recorded a trap in the prebuilt `macho` extractor: it answered this field as a single value, not a list. I updated the overview, variant axes, cues, conventions and pitfalls, and shortened the Days 15-19 entries.\n- **`reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md`**: marked Mach-O `seen D20` and added a forecast for D21-D23. That covers real universal binaries, the \"archives\" side (`ar` static libraries, macOS `.pkg`/`.dmg`, `.app` bundles), a cross-file architecture-support question, and the next format family. I added seven atlas rows (122-128), updated the Mach-O cue line, and kept the cues section at 60 lines.\n- **Readiness gaps**: I dropped `macho-header` and moved the ELF gaps down to priority 2. I added 9 new gaps: `macho-fat-slice-sets`, `ar-static-archives`, `macos-xar-pkg-dmg`, `macos-app-bundle-plist`, `macho-fleet-synthesis`, `macho-arch-name-vocab`, `msix-appx-arch`, `cpio-payloads` and `jar-manifest-class-versions`. Together with `elf-core-ko-firmware` that makes 10 prebuild gaps not yet built (the minimum is 8), and the JSON block still parses with the same keys."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":389,"cache_read_input_tokens":121865,"cache_creation":{"ephemer